{"name":"Coconut Cream","hex":"#e1dabb","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"coconut cream","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A thicker, more heavily flavoured version of coconut milk, with similarity to thick cream instead of milk.","Coconut-flavoured whipped cream. (Can we add an example for this sense?)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coconut_cream"}],"entries":[{"title":"Coconut Cream (mango)","blocks":[{"text":"The 'Coconut Cream' mango is a named mango cultivar that originated in south Florida."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coconut_Cream_(mango)"},{"title":"Coconut cream","blocks":[{"text":"Coconut cream is similar to coconut milk, but is thicker due to a higher concentration of coconut and a lower amount of water in a ratio of about 4:1. Coconut cream is used as an ingredient in cooking, and has an unsweetened flavor."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Coconut_cream_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Coconut_cream_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coconut_cream"},{"title":"Coconut","blocks":[{"text":"The coconut is a member of the palm family (Arecaceae) and the only living species of the genus Cocos. The term \"coconut\" can denote the whole coconut palm tree or the large hard fruit. Originally native to the Southeast Asia, New Guinea, and the Southwestern Pacific, they are ubiquitous in coastal tropical regions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Cocos_nucifera_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-187.jpg/330px-Cocos_nucifera_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-187.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coconut"},{"title":"Cream","blocks":[{"text":"Cream is a dairy product composed of the higher-fat layer skimmed from the top of milk before homogenization. The butterfat, which is less dense, rises to the top and is skimmed off, resulting in gravity cream. The industrial production of cream instead uses centrifugal separators to make separator cream. Cream is often sold in grades defined by their butterfat content. It contains high levels of saturated fat, in ascending proportion from light cream to heavy cream."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/01_Mmm..._Apple_Crisp_with_Whipped_Cream.jpg/330px-01_Mmm..._Apple_Crisp_with_Whipped_Cream.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cream"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Coco3wjf.JPG/500px-Coco3wjf.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Coco3wjf.JPG/1280px-Coco3wjf.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Coco3wjf.JPG/500px-Coco3wjf.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Coconut milk is a component of coconut cream","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACoco3wjf.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Coconut_4.jpg/500px-Coconut_4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Coconut_4.jpg/1280px-Coconut_4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Coconut_4.jpg/500px-Coconut_4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACoconut_4.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Sea_View_from_himsori_bangladesh_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-Sea_View_from_himsori_bangladesh_%28cr